    {
      "title": "Connection Pools: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Connection Pools: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Pool Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==pool== keeps a **fixed set** of open DB connections and lends them out",
                "New TCP + auth connection per query is {red:slow}",
                "The server ==caps connections==, so unbounded opens fail"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Lifecycle and Options",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Acquire",
                    "sub": "client from pool",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Query",
                    "sub": "run statements",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Release",
                    "sub": "back to pool",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "All clients busy: requests ==queue== until one frees",
                "Or the acquire timeout fires and the request {red:errors}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "pg option",
                "Default",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`max`",
                  "==10==",
                  "Most clients in the pool"
                ],
                [
                  "`idleTimeoutMillis`",
                  "==10000==",
                  "Idle client closed after this"
                ],
                [
                  "`connectionTimeoutMillis`",
                  "==0==",
                  "Acquire wait; 0 = **wait forever**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Sizing and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==instances × max== must stay **below** server `max_connections`",
                "Postgres default `max_connections` = ==100==",
                "Set `connectionTimeoutMillis` so a full pool fails fast"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "// db.js: created once at startup",
                "import pg from 'pg';",
                "export const pool = new pg.Pool({",
                "  max: 10,",
                "  connectionTimeoutMillis: 2000,",
                "});"
              ],
              "note": "every module imports this one pool"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "One Pool per process",
              "text": "A new `Pool` per request or per module import **leaks connections**. Create one at startup and share it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Parameterised Queries with pg",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Parameterised Queries with pg",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Placeholders",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`pool.query(text, values)` with ==$1, $2== placeholders",
                "Values travel **separately** from the SQL text",
                "Input is never parsed as SQL: ==no injection==",
                "Rows in `result.rows`, count in `result.rowCount`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const result = await pool.query(",
                "  'SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1 AND active = $2',",
                "  [email, true]",
                ");",
                "console.log(result.rows, result.rowCount);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Values, Not Identifiers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Position",
                "Can be $1?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Value in WHERE / INSERT",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Table or column name",
                  "{red:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "ORDER BY direction",
                  "{red:no}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Whitelist== identifiers in code",
                "Or build them with `format` and ==%I==",
                "Pass only the checked name into the SQL text"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`WHERE id = ${id}` is ==SQL injection==, even if the value 'looks' safe",
                "`pool.query` per statement in a transaction: each call may use a **different connection**"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const client = await pool.connect();",
                "try {",
                "  await client.query('BEGIN');",
                "  // queries on client, not pool",
                "  await client.query('COMMIT');",
                "} catch (e) { await client.query('ROLLBACK'); throw e;",
                "} finally { client.release(); }"
              ],
              "note": "dedicated client for a transaction"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Release the client",
              "text": "Always `client.release()` in ==finally==, or the pool leaks connections."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Transactions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Transactions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a transaction is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==transaction== groups statements: all **commit** or all **roll back** (ACID)",
                "Every statement must run on the ==same connection==",
                "`pool.query` may pick a different connection each call, so it cannot hold a transaction"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. pg pattern",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const client = await pool.connect();",
                "try {",
                "  await client.query('BEGIN');",
                "  // all statements use client",
                "  await client.query('COMMIT');",
                "} catch (e) {",
                "  await client.query('ROLLBACK'); throw e;",
                "} finally { client.release(); }"
              ],
              "note": "release() in finally, even after ROLLBACK"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Prisma and Drizzle",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Prisma",
                "Drizzle"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Batch",
                  "`$transaction([op1, op2])`",
                  "n/a"
                ],
                [
                  "Interactive",
                  "`$transaction(async (tx) => {...})`",
                  "`db.transaction(async (tx) => {...})`"
                ],
                [
                  "Timeout",
                  "default ==5s==",
                  "n/a"
                ],
                [
                  "Rollback",
                  "throw inside",
                  "throw, or `tx.rollback()`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Calling `db` / `prisma` instead of `tx` runs that query ==outside== the transaction",
                "Holding a transaction open across slow network calls **pins** a pooled connection"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Inside the callback",
              "text": "Use only ==tx== (or the dedicated `client`). Keep transactions short."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
