    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You run `pool.query('BEGIN')`, then two `pool.query` updates, then `pool.query('COMMIT')`. The second update fails. What gets rolled back?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Possibly nothing: each `pool.query` can use a **different connection**.",
                "`BEGIN` may sit on one connection and the updates on others, so there is no real transaction.",
                "Fix: `pool.connect()`, run every statement on that `client`, `client.release()` in `finally`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Inside `prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {...})` you write `await prisma.order.create(...)`, then throw. Is the order rolled back?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No. `prisma` is not `tx`, so that query runs **outside** the transaction.",
                "It commits on its own. Only queries made through `tx` roll back."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "On SIGTERM a handler calls `await pool.end()`, but the process never exits. A route did `pool.connect()` and threw before `release()`. Why the hang?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`pool.end()` waits for every checked-out client to be returned.",
                "That client was never released, so shutdown waits forever.",
                "Fix: always `client.release()` in a `finally` block."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
